doc:sch-1-sec-228a-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "228A(1) The things authorised by a search warrant—additional things" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A *search warrant authorises the *executing officer or a *person assisting to *seize a *digital asset if:  Seizing digital assets  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1 No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024 (a) in the course of exercising powers under this Part, the executing officer or a person assisting finds one or more things that suggest the existence of the digital asset; and (b) the executing officer or a person assisting reasonably suspects the digital asset to be: (i) *tainted property to which the warrant relates; or (ii) *evidential material in relation to property to which the warrant relates; or (iii) evidential material (within the meaning of the Crimes Act 1914) relating to an *indictable offence; and (c) the executing officer or a person assisting reasonably suspects that seizing the digital asset is necessary to prevent the digital asset’s concealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an offence. Note: For the purposes of paragraph (a), the digital asset need not be found at the premises. Data accessed using powers under this Part may suggest the existence of the digital asset. For example, a thing suggesting the existence of the digital asset could be found by accessing data not held at the premises: see section 245. Use of electronic equipment etc. to seize a digital asset etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-228a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "228A(2) The things authorised by a search warrant—additional things"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-228a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A *search warrant authorises the *executing officer or a *person assisting: (a) to use: (i) a computer, or *data storage device, found in the course of a search authorised under the warrant; or (ii) a *telecommunications facility operated or provided by the Commonwealth or a *carrier; or (iii) any other electronic equipment; or (iv) a data storage device; for the purpose of *seizing a *digital asset under the warrant; and (b) if necessary to achieve that purpose—to add, copy, delete or alter *data in the computer or device mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i); and (c) if it is reasonable in all the circumstances to do so for the purpose of seizing a digital asset under the warrant:  Schedule 1  Seizing digital assets" ;
    skos:definition "(2) A *search warrant authorises the *executing officer or a *person assisting: (a) to use: (i) a computer, or *data storage device, found in the course of a search authorised under the warrant; or (ii) a *telecommunications facility operated or provided by the Commonwealth or a *carrier; or (iii) any other electronic equipment; or (iv) a data storage device; for the purpose of *seizing a *digital asset under the warrant; and (b) if necessary to achieve that purpose—to add, copy, delete or alter *data in the computer or device mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i); and (c) if it is reasonable in all the circumstances to do so for the purpose of seizing a digital asset under the warrant:  Schedule 1  Seizing digital assets"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5a8b4897b79c0e5d4d3d16c01a25cacd51a8ea9383383507123a620fc6be51e1" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-228a ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorises use of computer, data storage device, telecommunications facility, and other electronic equipment for seizing digital assets." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf, p.18" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-228a-ss-2-norm .
