concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42 Section 338"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-42 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: carrier means: (a) a carrier within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997; or (b) a carriage service provider within the meaning of that Act. communication in transit means a communication (within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997) passing over a telecommunications network (within the meaning of that Act).  Seizing digital assets  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1 No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024 digital asset means: (a) a digital representation of value or rights (including rights to property), the ownership of which is evidenced cryptographically and that is held and transferred electronically by: (i) a type of distributed ledger technology; or (ii) another distributed cryptographically verifiable data structure; or (b) a right or thing prescribed by the regulations; but does not include any right or thing that, under the regulations, is taken not to be a digital asset for the purposes of this Act. seize, for a *digital asset, has a meaning affected by subsection 228A(6). telecommunications facility means a facility within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: carrier means: (a) a carrier within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997; or (b) a carriage service provider within the meaning of that Act. communication in transit means a communication (within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997) passing over a telecommunications network (within the meaning of that Act).  Seizing digital assets  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1 No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024 digital asset means: (a) a digital representation of value or rights (including rights to property), the ownership of which is evidenced cryptographically and that is held and transferred electronically by: (i) a type of distributed ledger technology; or (ii) another distributed cryptographically verifiable data structure; or (b) a right or thing prescribed by the regulations; but does not include any right or thing that, under the regulations, is taken not to be a digital asset for the purposes of this Act. seize, for a *digital asset, has a meaning affected by subsection 228A(6). telecommunications facility means a facility within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1997."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c0fa6d7be84da91f276ac547f7da8773b1c600b47b1ee1464f039a32e3fbb4ae" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines carrier and communication in transit." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf, p.24" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-42-norm .
