doc:sch-4-sec-174 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "174 Co-operation with agencies—Telecommunications" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(Interception and Access) Act 1979 If, before the commencement of this Schedule, a power was exercised or a function or duty was performed by the Communications Access Co-ordinator under Chapter 5 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 on a day, then, on and after that commencement, a Communications Access Coordinator is taken to have exercised the power or performed the function or duty on that day.  Schedule 5  Information sharing between integrity agencies and oversight bodies  Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024 No. 93, 2024" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-4-sec-175 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "175 Civil penalty proceedings—Telecommunications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-175 ;
    values:originalText "(Interception and Access) Act 1979 If, immediately before the commencement of this Schedule, the Communications Access Co-ordinator was an applicant for a civil penalty under the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014 in relation to a provision of Part 8 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, the Communications Access Coordinator is substituted for the Communications Access Co-ordinator as the applicant on and after that commencement.  Information sharing between integrity agencies and oversight bodies  Schedule 5  No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024" ;
    skos:definition "(Interception and Access) Act 1979 If, immediately before the commencement of this Schedule, the Communications Access Co-ordinator was an applicant for a civil penalty under the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014 in relation to a provision of Part 8 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, the Communications Access Coordinator is substituted for the Communications Access Co-ordinator as the applicant on and after that commencement.  Information sharing between integrity agencies and oversight bodies  Schedule 5  No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "415ba20afdf62043eef5ff52e5fd0833dc5727b148edbabb8f95782293649ee5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Substitution of Communications Access Co-ordinator as applicant for civil penalty under Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014." ;
