concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-7-sec-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Dictionary in the Criminal Code (definition of hors de"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-1 ;
    values:originalText "combat) Repeal the definition, substitute: hors de combat: a person is hors de combat if: (a) any of the following apply: (i) the person is in the power of an adverse party; (ii) the person clearly expresses an intention to surrender; (iii) the person has been rendered unconscious or is otherwise incapacitated by wounds or sickness and is therefore incapable of defending himself or herself; and (b) the person abstains from any hostile act and does not attempt to escape.  Meaning of hors de combat  Schedule 7 Application of amendment  Part 2 No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024" ;
    skos:definition "combat) Repeal the definition, substitute: hors de combat: a person is hors de combat if: (a) any of the following apply: (i) the person is in the power of an adverse party; (ii) the person clearly expresses an intention to surrender; (iii) the person has been rendered unconscious or is otherwise incapacitated by wounds or sickness and is therefore incapable of defending himself or herself; and (b) the person abstains from any hostile act and does not attempt to escape.  Meaning of hors de combat  Schedule 7 Application of amendment  Part 2 No. 93, 2024 Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "296b750b38e449897c0506e671ccb7f8a6a688381642a43d93a7aa2763e537cf" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of hors de combat" ;
